<title>SPAIN: Santander, BBV cut prime rates.</title>
<headline>Santander, BBV cut prime rates.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish banks Banco Santander and Banco Bilbao Vizcaya both reduced their prime rates by a quarter point on Friday immediately following the Bank of Spain's decision to lower its key rate to six percent from 6.25 percent.</p>
<p>Santander said it cut its prime rate to 7.75 percent from eight percent.</p>
<p>BBV said it cut its prime rate to 8.25 percent from 8.50 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
